<article class="env-lemma" id="03H1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03H1">Lemma <span data-tag="03H1">115.11.1</span>.</a> Let $(R, \mathfrak m, \kappa )$ be a local ring. Let $X \subset \mathbf{P}^ n_ R$ be a closed subscheme. Assume that $R = \Gamma (X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$. Then the special fibre $X_ k$ is geometrically connected. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of More on Morphisms, Theorem <a href="/tag/03H2" data-tag="03H2">37.53.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>